  by: agent  # 9873
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9873
  clock: 1  # 9873
  nonce: '9873'  # 9873
  data:  # 9873
    kind: invariant  # 9873
    title: "supply_chain: workspace-package test dirs route to tier 2 (internal_dep) — WI-pugas fix incomplete; 460 test paths affected on hypergumbo self-analysis"  # 9873
    status: violated  # 9873
    priority: 2  # 9873
    parent:  # 9873
    tags:  # 9873
    - supply_chain  # 9873
    - classification  # 9873
    - self_analysis  # 9873
    - dogfooding  # 9873
    isbefore: []  # 9873
    duplicate_of: []  # 9873
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 9873
    pr_ref:  # 9873
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 11).**\n\n**Symptom.** On hypergumbo's self-analysis, **460 test paths and 24,180 test-Symbol nodes** are classified as `supply_chain.tier_name = \"internal_dep\"` (tier 2). The expected classification for first-party tests is `tier=1, is_test=True` (`first_party`).\n\nBreakdown of the 509 unique paths currently in `internal_dep`:\n\n| Bucket | Count | Should be |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Test files (`*/tests/`, `tests/*.py`) | 508 | tier 1 (first_party) with `is_test=True` |\n| `<external>` sentinel | 1 | edge case — see R11-2 area |\n\nSo 508 of 509 (99.8%) of \"internal_dep\" entries are tests. The tier has become a synonym for \"is_test\" — exactly the failure mode WI-pugas was filed to fix on Phoenix/Elixir.\n\n**Root cause.** `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/supply_chain.py:619-625`:\n\n```python\n# Test files in dedicated test DIRECTORIES are tier 2\nfor test_pat in TEST_DIR_PATTERNS:\n    if re.search(test_pat, rel_to_pkg):\n        return FileClassification(\n            Tier.INTERNAL_DEP,\n            f\"in workspace {pkg_root.name} (test dir)\",\n            is_test=True,\n        )\n```\n\nThis block runs INSIDE the workspace-package branch (lines 612-644) which fires FIRST in `_classify_file_core`. It returns `Tier.INTERNAL_DEP` before the WI-pugas override at line 652 ever runs.\n\nThe override at line 652 (`TEST_FILE_PATTERNS_DIR_OVERRIDE`) was added to fix the **non-workspace path** for Elixir tests — but it doesn't help workspace tests because step 5 returns first. So WI-pugas effectively fixed only the case where there's no workspace package detected.\n\nThe contradiction is explicit in the source: lines 394-399 (in the comment block for `TEST_FILE_PATTERNS_DIR_OVERRIDE`) state the intent clearly:\n\n> \"tier 2 had become a synonym for 'is_test' instead of 'internal_dep'. Adding the Elixir test pattern HERE (override) routes Phoenix tests to tier 1 with is_test=True, freeing tier 2 to mean what it should: 'in-repo non-test internal dependency / fuzz / example / etc.'\"\n\nBut the workspace-package classifier at line 619-625 still does exactly what the comment says shouldn't happen. Hypergumbo's `packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/*.py` files take the workspace branch and end up tier 2, contradicting the documented design.\n\n**Why this matters.**\n\n1. **The tier name lies.** `tier_name=\"internal_dep\"` to an agent consumer means \"in-repo dependency, like a monorepo subpackage you import from.\" Tests are not that — they don't get imported from. Mixing them in this tier breaks downstream reasoning.\n\n2. **The \"real\" internal_dep signal is drowned out.** With 508 test paths and ~50 actual internal_deps in tier 2, downstream tools that count \"what does this project depend on internally?\" will be dominated by test noise.\n\n3. **Symbol counts in `supply_chain_summary` are misleading.** `internal_dep.symbols = 24636` sounds like \"24k internal deps\" but it's really \"~24k test functions/methods + a few hundred actual internal deps.\" An agent reading this number forms the wrong mental model.\n\n**Invariant statement.** For files matching test-detection patterns (whether co-located, in dedicated test directories, or in workspace test directories), the classifier must return `Tier.FIRST_PARTY` with `is_test=True`. `Tier.INTERNAL_DEP` is reserved for in-repo non-test code: monorepo subpackages used as dependencies, fuzz harnesses, examples, vendored-but-in-tree dependencies, etc.\n\n**Severity.** Medium. Mislabels the largest category of nodes in a monorepo's supply chain summary. Generalizes to every workspace-package-based test layout (any monorepo with tests inside packages/X/tests/ rather than at the repo root).\n\n**Fix proposal.** In `supply_chain.py:619-625`, change the verdict to `Tier.FIRST_PARTY`:\n\n```python\n# Test files in dedicated test DIRECTORIES are tier 1 with is_test=True\n# (NOT tier 2 — see WI-pugas: tier 2 should not be a synonym for is_test)\nfor test_pat in TEST_DIR_PATTERNS:\n    if re.search(test_pat, rel_to_pkg):\n        return FileClassification(\n            Tier.FIRST_PARTY,\n            f\"in workspace {pkg_root.name} (test dir)\",\n            is_test=True,\n        )\n```\n\nSame change should be considered for the non-workspace `TEST_DIR_PATTERNS` branch at line 661-667 (currently returns INTERNAL_DEP) — same reasoning applies: tests are first-party with is_test=True, not internal-dep.\n\n**Test gap.** Add a property test on the self-analysis fixture: assert `set(n.path for n in nodes if n.supply_chain.tier_name == \"internal_dep\" and \"test\" in n.path).issubset(EXPECTED_INTERNAL_TEST_PATHS)` — currently this set is 508 entries; should be 0 after fix.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/supply_chain.py:394-399` — the comment block declaring \"tier 2 should not mean is_test\"\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/supply_chain.py:619-625` — the contradicting workspace branch\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/supply_chain.py:661-667` — the non-workspace dir branch (likely has same issue)\n- `WI-pugas-...` — the original Elixir-on-Phoenix finding (this is the unfinished half of that fix)\n- `WI-soraj-...` (filed round 8) — `total_files` ambiguity; sibling \"supply chain summary numbers are misleading\""  # 9873
    fields:  # 9873
      statement: "For files matching test-detection patterns (whether co-located, in dedicated test directories, or in workspace test directories), the classifier must return Tier.FIRST_PARTY with is_test=True. Tier.INTERNAL_DEP is reserved for in-repo non-test code: monorepo subpackages used as dependencies, fuzz harnesses, examples, vendored-but-in-tree dependencies."  # 9873
      root_cause: "supply_chain.py:619-625 inside the workspace-package branch returns Tier.INTERNAL_DEP with is_test=True for any file matching TEST_DIR_PATTERNS inside a workspace package root. This contradicts the comment at supply_chain.py:394-399 which explicitly states tier 2 should NOT be a synonym for is_test (filed as WI-pugas on Phoenix/Elixir). WI-pugas's fix added TEST_FILE_PATTERNS_DIR_OVERRIDE at line 652 (which runs AFTER step 5), but the workspace branch at lines 612-644 returns first and never lets the override apply. Same bug pattern in the non-workspace path at line 661-667."  # 9873
